  "body": "Porting from https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=28925\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-a-element:following-hyperlinks-2-2 calls https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#following-hyperlinks-2 passing a \"hyperlink suffix\" that is a string like \"`?5,10`\".\r\n\r\nStep 11 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#following-hyperlinks-2 appends the string to a URL record, which doesn't make sense.\r\n\r\nWe need tests (and optionally source code inspection) to determine what exactly is done. Here are some possibilities I could imagine:\r\n\r\n- The input URL string is parsed, then serialized, then the string is appended, then the result is parsed again, then fetched.\r\n- The input URL string gets the hyperlink suffix appended, then parsed, then fetched.\r\n- The input URL string is parsed, then any query component is replaced with the hyperlink suffix.\r\n- The input URL string is parsed, and then the hyperlink suffix is appended to the fragment, query, or path, depending on which of those is non-null.\r\n- ...",
